:: EV_a3_swapback_reminder_a
The Redmi buzzes. Kavya: //Temple. 7:30. Don't be late   I want my hands back and you want yours.//

You look at Kavya's hands. The silver ring. The short shaped nails. Twelve hours of borrowed dexterity, and a small, stupid flicker of something like loss.

<<hubreturn>>


:: EV_a3_pooja_wa
<div class="alert-popup danger" style="position:static;max-width:none;margin-bottom:1rem;">💬 Pooja Pagal 🙄</div>

<div class="chat-log">
<div class="msg them">Bhaiya Sunday confirm? Aai ne mutton le liya. Also sheera. She's cooking like you're coming back from war<span class="gloss-en">Brother, is Sunday confirmed? Aai bought mutton.</span></div>
<div class="msg me">Haan confirm. Tell Aai not to cook for army.<span class="gloss-en">Yes, confirmed.</span></div>
<div class="msg them">omg you replied in MINUTES. Usually you take HOURS</div>
<div class="msg them">Also you said "not to cook for army." You usually say "Aai ko bol zyada mat banana." Same meaning, different words.<span class="gloss-en">You'd normally say "tell Aai not to make too much."</span></div>
<div class="msg them">I'm watching you 👀</div>
</div>

A seventeen-year-old just flagged a linguistic anomaly in your impersonation within three messages. You don't reply again. Some tests you fail by continuing.

<<run setup.stat("pooja_suspicion", 3, "kavya")>>
<<hubreturn>>


:: EV_a3_aai_call
<div class="alert-popup danger" style="position:static;max-width:none;margin-bottom:1rem;">📞 Aai ❤️</div>

You can't not answer. Arjun always answers his mother.

<div class="dialogue">"Beta, kha liya? ... Sirf dosa? Ande kha, protein chahiye. ... Sunday confirm hai na? Pooja ne bola tu jaldi reply kar raha hai. Kuch hua kya?"<span class="gloss-en">Son, have you eaten? ... Just a dosa? Eat eggs, you need protein. ... Sunday's confirmed, right? Pooja says you're replying fast. Did something happen?</span></div>

"Kuch nahi Aai. Bas class mein free tha."<span class="gloss-en">Nothing, Aai. Just had a free period.</span>

<div class="dialogue">"Hmm. Tera voice thoda alag lag raha hai. Sardi toh nahi lagi?"<span class="gloss-en">Hmm. Your voice sounds a little different. You haven't caught a cold?</span></div>

Same vocal cords. Same pitch. But a mother is hearing something underneath   the cadence, the faintly Tamil syntax you build Hindi sentences with. Mothers are debugging tools, and this one just logged a warning.

"Voice theek hai, Aai. Neend puri nahi hui."<span class="gloss-en">My voice is fine, Aai. Didn't sleep enough.</span>

<<run setup.stat("aai_suspicion", 1, "kavya")>>
<<hubreturn>>


:: EV_a3_rohit_gym
Rohit stands, cracks his back, announces "leg day extension" as if his quads filed a formal request, and leaves. The door closes. His footsteps recede down the stairs.

The room is yours. The laptop is yours. Two hours.

<<hubreturn>>


:: EV_a3_swapback_reminder_k
Arjun's phone buzzes. Meera, via the Samsung: //7:30. Pataleshwar. He needs his body and you need yours. And Kavya   thank you. For the CS classes. For all of it.//

You look at the clock in the corner of the borrowed screen. The keyboard under your hands. Soon this stops.

<<hubreturn>>


:: day3_swapback
<div class="intimate"><span class="tag">The swap-back</span>
<<img "pataleshwar_dawn.png" "Pataleshwar, evening">>
The circle again, drawn in the last light. The thread. The mantra in reverse   the wrench comes and this time you brace for it, like jumping into cold water the second time.

Black. White. Colours resolving.

<<if $pov is "arjun">>You open your eyes and the first thing you feel is your cock. Right there. The familiar weight you never once appreciated in twenty-one years. Your chest is flat. Your lungs expand fully. You're taller   the temple walls are back at eye level.

And, strangely, a flicker of loss. Kavya's body was terrifying and alien and also a country you'd barely entered, a language you spoke for twelve hours and were just starting to understand.

"Tera dissection class bhayanak hai,"<span class="gloss-en">Your dissection class is horrifying.</span> you tell Kavya, who's patting herself down   face, chest, hips, the body-audit of a woman reclaiming her property.

<div class="dialogue">"Tere Rohit ko control karo. Also your bike's in VIT lot B, keys in your jacket. I didn't scratch it."<span class="gloss-en">Get your Rohit under control.</span></div>
<<else>>You open your eyes and your breasts are BACK   two familiar masses dropping into position, the Clovia underwire clamping down. Twelve hours flat-chested and free, and now the whole production returns.

The world rises. You're looking up at the Nandi statue again. Small again. And between your legs: the absence where a warm, present, slightly ridiculous weight used to be. Not wrong. Familiar. But the familiarity has a new texture now.

"Your laptop is beautiful," you tell Arjun, and the tears come, fast, Kavya's zero-latency system firing. "I wrote two thousand lines of production code. I //coded//, Arjun. On a real keyboard."

<div class="dialogue">"Also your Pulsar is a death machine and I love it."</div>
<</if>>

You both laugh. Real laughter, in your own voices, bouncing off 1,500-year-old stone. Tomorrow you do this again. The thought is terrifying and inevitable in equal measure.
</div>\
<<run setup.setBody("arjun", "arjun")>>\
<<run setup.setBody("kavya", "kavya")>>\
